# Keep the image built from package-lock.json, not from a developer's disk.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and only then `COPY . .`. Without this file that
# COPY would lay the host's own node_modules over the tree the lockfile just
# installed, so the image would be built against whatever happened to be
# installed locally. A fresh CI checkout has no node_modules, which is why the
# defect never shows up there.
#
# Over-excluding breaks the image as surely as under-excluding: nginx.conf,
# package*.json, angular.json, federation*.js, tsconfig*.json and src/ are all
# read by the build and must stay in.

# Installed/derived trees, regenerated inside the image.
**/node_modules
.angular
dist
out-tsc
coverage

# VCS, CI and editor metadata, never read by the build.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp

# Local env/secrets must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test and report output.
test-results
**/*.log
